                    <p class=MsoNormal><span style="font-family:仿宋;mso-bidi-font-family:'Times New Roman';font-size:12.0000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><font face="仿宋"><p><em>Introduction to Vaccinology</em> systematically covers fundamental knowledge, principles, and the evolution of vaccines, highlighting their pivotal role in preventing infectious diseases. The course explores vaccine development strategies, production quality control, clinical safety and efficacy, alongside global immunization programs, public health policies, and responses to emerging outbreaks. Students will gain insights into immune response mechanisms, stay abreast of cutting-edge advancements, and build a solid foundation for careers in public health. Join us in unraveling the science of vaccines and safeguarding global health. ​</p></font></span><span style="font-family:'Times New Roman';mso-fareast-font-family:仿宋;font-size:10.5000pt;
mso-font-kerning:1.0000pt;"><o:p></o:p></span></p>
                </td>
            </tr>
